{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_270c260c280bd20f06162d692613176d1a8e56665778f643c12b5e6a57eb9c75","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"ouijit/ouijit@b868ef792dc7 snapshot 6945b93047da6ab2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0c5f6453cba131004fec43631357be79f4b401a11af6ec19b0df36af75f30e7f"],"source_ids":["src_ec4eba6ea092520d92853ffde0d878e8"],"text":"Ouijit shadows agent binaries on PATH to inject lifecycle hooks and a CLI reference into each session, letting agents create tasks, advance the board, and open panels without setup.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5bab2cc5a333c8b903f90830f338ddf4120029d06ab19c3b5146b7f43dd22a08","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"ouijit/ouijit@b868ef792dc7 snapshot 6945b93047da6ab2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a7a4d2ee06b602887ec7c7cde3e82d771d98b12805bd12e7a21c1c9b06136c51"],"source_ids":["src_ec4eba6ea092520d92853ffde0d878e8"],"text":"Tasks live on a kanban board; moving a card between To Do, In Progress, In Review, and Done fires a matching lifecycle hook, and starting a task creates an isolated git worktree.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5f894fe31fd20819adc5d4991dd48df00cd55b4ec4294797c35a2963756ceaff","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"ouijit/ouijit@b868ef792dc7 snapshot 6945b93047da6ab2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_597dc8a22d70950f75f3c1aa09a054f7c2bbef73c86a9882ced7ab0ec04f3013"],"source_ids":["src_ec4eba6ea092520d92853ffde0d878e8"],"text":"Terminals are cards in a stack with attachable panel tabs: a script runner, a web preview, and markdown files with Mermaid diagrams; non-task shells get their own board strip.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_64406e474e733694ef6b6da5a3d40c5f6edd12499e028256183f06f94f8727b6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"ouijit/ouijit@b868ef792dc7 snapshot 6945b93047da6ab2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_acf3a165e2b951b1a23d4fdecc4f4e407a3f91c4aa6e5c40cabb05c7edec898b"],"source_ids":["src_ec4eba6ea092520d92853ffde0d878e8"],"text":"An experimental GitHub surface provides a pull request inbox, locally staged review comments, and merging, driven by the `gh` CLI with `gh auth login` as the only setup.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_71f73c843a2d483520389ce9d9367ae6786f45fe35cd7726c45c01135a4956f0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"ouijit/ouijit@b868ef792dc7 snapshot 6945b93047da6ab2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bbb9953cbb01c6e3f32f3f093ee068dfc40d4a26f193ba655cf1a96a9e6af215"],"source_ids":["src_ec4eba6ea092520d92853ffde0d878e8"],"text":"Ouijit is a task and terminal manager for running coding agents in parallel, where each task gets its own git worktree and terminal, with lifecycle hooks launching the agent CLI.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7b8457e7f488730e822425c84f102b052d97ab59acf8fe44ee96d9dc63e7d25e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"ouijit/ouijit@b868ef792dc7 snapshot 6945b93047da6ab2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_acf3a165e2b951b1a23d4fdecc4f4e407a3f91c4aa6e5c40cabb05c7edec898b"],"source_ids":["src_ec4eba6ea092520d92853ffde0d878e8"],"text":"Each task terminal shows a diff of its worktree against a merge target, uncommitted changes, or a chosen base, with word-level highlighting and per-line notes routed to the agent in that worktree.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8a85cf2bcf2aadd90fbe7a07e04d205da3e44c728452a2d3cdba0e5086a94932","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"ouijit/ouijit@b868ef792dc7 snapshot 6945b93047da6ab2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a1b751d8652d6da717094b5a29f8f098a767203b6c004d613c6b377ff3343d26","slc_cb3d116d59c1998edf044a50cfffffa67411cc31e1081621b42a4462baa00a39","slc_e83cfa042dc6029f40aa44a0ddcebfda8aa0e172c28a19f1bce06cddb8ecc309"],"source_ids":["src_ec4eba6ea092520d92853ffde0d878e8"],"text":"The project is free and open source under AGPL-3.0, with no account, sign-in, or telemetry, and distributes self-contained builds for macOS (Apple Silicon/Intel) and Linux x64.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a2ffbd6fb77fddc94805bfe8e48e5e01bdb12b837d5cefc5686ed4a93d1120c9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"ouijit/ouijit@b868ef792dc7 snapshot 6945b93047da6ab2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6caab8da91a63fc1f3c068e6e91ef5ed1275ed9e27ffd2bd7791cab38afc1b4e","slc_e7bbb86dee8c3ffe93c39ce8ceaba52ca2aa5b278866ecd758f0b7c95f5e7b8c"],"source_ids":["src_ec4eba6ea092520d92853ffde0d878e8"],"text":"Quitting saves the session, and the next launch offers to restore its terminals in their worktrees, panels included; all data is stored locally in SQLite.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a898bebb64a0aad82979737d442811239b0cda75bffbb7a81493f1732d499b12","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"ouijit/ouijit@b868ef792dc7 snapshot 6945b93047da6ab2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_cd9df417c5340ee1269558a684fc119c498a1304fa57824f0cd3934fe6b1675d"],"source_ids":["src_ec4eba6ea092520d92853ffde0d878e8"],"text":"Any terminal can run sandboxed: in a Lima VM mounting only the task's worktree, in place under Seatbelt/Landlock via nono (experimental), or under a user-supplied launcher (experimental).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:11:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_65ebf8f0ece440de97aa8df8fa885f65"}
